# MCSP Structural Scaffold Carrier 0.25

Status: Constructive bootstrap design
Qualification: Under Conditional Experiment
Parent: Continuous Pre-Settlement Scaffolding 0.24

## 1. Purpose

Provide a machine-representable scaffold form for continuous pre-settlement and canonical normalization.

This carrier is NOT the final MCSP-native encoding.

It is bootstrap scaffolding used to discover the encoding MCSP must eventually describe for itself.

## 2. Principle

Names may locate records.

Names SHALL NOT determine semantic equivalence.

Two independently authored scaffolds may use different documentary identifiers and still normalize to the same semantic structure.

## 3. Record form

A scaffold record provisionally contains:

    record {
        local_id
        qualification
        applicability
        commitments[]
        relations[]
        dimensions[]
        dependencies[]
        extensions[]
        realization_constraints[]
        unresolved[]
    }

local_id is documentary only.

## 4. Commitment

A commitment records a pre-settlement:

    commitment {
        local_id
        structure
        materiality
        applicability
        qualification
    }

The semantic authority is the qualified structure, not local_id.

## 5. Relation

A relation records structural participation:

    relation {
        kind_structure
        participants[]
        applicability
        qualification
    }

kind_structure must itself eventually be represented structurally.

A textual relation name is bootstrap metadata only.

## 6. Dimension status

Each applicable dimension records one of:

    PRESET
    CONSTRAINED
    OPEN
    REALIZATION_DEFINED
    UNSUPPORTED
    UNRESOLVED

The status vocabulary is bootstrap qualification notation and must later be self-described.

## 7. Normalization objective

Normalization SHALL remove documentary differences that do not change qualified semantic structure.

Candidate normalization steps:

1. discard non-semantic documentary labels;
2. retain qualification/applicability boundaries;
3. reduce derived aliases to their qualified structural definitions;
4. order structural records deterministically;
5. canonicalize relation participant ordering only where the relation is qualified order-insensitive;
6. retain order where material;
7. retain open/constrained/preset dimension status;
8. retain unresolved residue;
9. produce a deterministic structural form;
10. derive a structural digest only after deterministic form exists.

A digest is evidence of normalized representation equality, not semantic proof by itself.

## 8. Equivalence

Two scaffolds are candidate-equivalent when their normalized qualified structures are isomorphic under documentary identifier renaming while preserving:

    material commitments
    applicability
    relation structure
    material order
    dimension status
    qualification
    unresolved semantic residue

Identifier equality is neither necessary nor sufficient.

## 9. Canonicalization

A CANONICAL may be represented as a normalized qualified pre-settlement scaffold.

Thus:

    CANONICAL
      := qualified reusable normalized scaffold
         with stable material invariant

This remains a constructive definition.

## 10. Continuous pre-settlement

A successor scaffold may add commitments while preserving inherited qualified commitments.

Provisional lineage:

    scaffold_n
      -> qualified refinement
      -> scaffold_n+1

The successor records:
- inherited structure;
- additions;
- explicit narrowing;
- superseded unqualified hypotheses;
- affected qualification.

Silent mutation is forbidden.

## 11. Orthogonalization

A dimension is an orthogonal candidate only if controlled scaffold variants can change that dimension while preserving selected other material commitments.

Therefore orthogonalization becomes testable over normalized scaffolds.

## 12. Hardware independence

Hardware-specific realization records may differ substantially while projecting to the same normalized semantic scaffold.

That provides a structural target for hardware-independence qualification.

The normalized scaffold does not erase material hardware constraints when those constraints are part of the pre-settlement.

## 13. Anonymous condition

The carrier SHALL permit a determinate condition to participate without a human semantic name.

A local machine identifier may be necessary for representation, but it is not semantic identity.

This distinction is mandatory.

## 14. Bootstrap warning

This file still uses:
- textual field names;
- textual statuses;
- documentary ordering;
- external parser assumptions.

Therefore it does NOT satisfy MCSP self-description closure.

These dependencies must be progressively replaced by MCSP-described structure.

## 15. Next implementation

Create a minimal bootstrap scaffold data instance containing:
- the determinate-condition kernel candidate;
- pre-settlement;
- continuous refinement;
- canonical normalization obligations;
- open hardware/host dimensions.

Then implement deterministic normalization in C and test:
- renaming invariance;
- ordering invariance where non-material;
- ordering sensitivity where material;
- open-versus-preset sensitivity;
- qualification sensitivity;
- unresolved-residue sensitivity.

No runtime PASS is asserted by this specification.
